WEBVTT

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:10.300
Hey, do you…

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.600
Do you wanna play badminton?

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.860
I'm on the team.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.660
Wanna try playing with me?

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.700
You're so good, Shiratori!
Did you play back in elementary?

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.180
Uh, no…

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.540
Wanna join the team? We could be partners.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.380
And you're…

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.040
I'm Tachibana Azuma.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.360
Hi.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.760
Do you know what you'll do about high school?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.840
Yeah. Toba High is known for
its badminton team.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:14.740
Makes sense.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.020
You're going there too, right?

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.280
Where else would I go?

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.480
Don't forget that…

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.560
…together we're the strongest.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:05.440
[#04: Conflict]

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.900
[All-Japan Corporate Badminton Tournament]
[Day 1]

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:12.020
[Kimura Kohei vs. Saeki Sota]
Game. Match won by Saeki Sota

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:13.520
from Sunlight Beverage.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.220
You were awesome!

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:17.740
First game's ours!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.720
Don't get comfortable
just 'cause you won one game!

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.540
We're aiming for the top!

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.280
Yes, sir!

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.820
Oof, wouldn't want him to coach me.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:31.220
Sunlight Beverage really
burst onto the scene this year.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.520
Plus they won both sets
in their first doubles game.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:39.000
Did you hear that? People are
talking about our team!

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:39.740
Yeah!

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:45.220
The brawn of Miyazumi the veteran,
and the brains of Shiratori the newcomer.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.480
You'd never believe they
became partners just recently!

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:52.200
But we're only in round one,
so we've still got a long way to go.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.980
It's a national competition featuring
the 200 or so corporate badminton teams.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.940
For SB to get to the finals, they need to…

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.880
They need to beat seven other teams?! Gosh…

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.340
It sounds like a lot, but they'll get through
the first five rounds in the next three days.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.040
If everything goes well, they'll be up against
Tomari Transport in the fifth round.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.760
Won't be easy, that one!

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.760
Hang in there, guys!

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.060
[Isuzu Diner]

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.720
Cheers!

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.580
But we're playing tomorrow,
so no alcohol for us.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.280
Nothing like oolong tea after victory!

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.360
Toya, you didn't even play today.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.080
And that's thanks to you guys
winning both your games.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:39.120
Just you wait!
My racket will be on fire tomorrow!

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:44.620
They're kinda… awfully quiet today.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.600
It's the Scallion Ginger Ale.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.840
Oh right, they have to make a prototype
for the internal presentation.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:52.840
Yeah, that's not going so great.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.880
This is the data we got from our analysis.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:05.600
In summary, the more scallion qualities we add,
the less drinkable it becomes.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.240
Yeah, saw that coming from a mile away.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.560
Same here.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:12.450
May I?

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:19.500
Speaking for QA, it is only through
observing that new products meet all standards

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.900
that we can assure our customers' safety.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.840
I will not have you
ignoring that aspect of the product.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.920
I think the flavor's a priority…

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:34.020
Of course, we haven't
forgotten about meeting standards.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:37.160
But making scallions into a soft drink is, well…

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:43.440
Please give us some more time!
I know we can make this taste good!

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:47.100
I'm not sure we can trust your
standards for what "tastes good."

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.640
[Favorite drink: Natto Cola]

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.880
Why did it have to be Usuyama…

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.500
That guy has it out for Sales.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:57.520
Does your boss have to
have a stick up his ass all the time?

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:00.240
He takes his work very seriously, is all.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:01.500
Delish…

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:05.800
But how do we convert that flavor into a drink…

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:09.240
Might be good to learn
a little more about Fukaya scallions.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:11.520
They're so good…

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:16.640
They are, aren't they? We get them
directly from the farmers in Fukaya.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:21.200
Could you tell us more about them?

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.800
[All-Japan Corporate Badminton Tournament]
[Day 2]

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:33.880
Game. Match won by Takeda Koki and Saeki Toya
from Sunlight Beverage.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.900
Heck yeah!

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.200
They did it! They got through the fourth round!

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.800
They're finally facing Tomari tomorrow.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.420
Ah, yes, Tomari…

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:50.400
Smash shots delivered by those broad back
muscles developed by working in transport…

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.080
A super-aggressive team that excels
in low-altitude battles just short of the net…

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.860
Also known as the Golden Lions of the North…!

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.860
Players with a wild streak… We stan!

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:08.520
SB has never won as a team though…

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:11.100
Think they'll manage this year?

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:14.360
It's from Ninosaka.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.960
He's not coming today either, is he?

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.140
Enjoy working on your day off.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:22.540
Seriously, where's his team spirit…

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:24.540
He's consistent, if nothing else.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.920
Get lots of rest before tomorrow.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.660
Thank you for today.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.200
Shall we?

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:31.960
Yes.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.720
See you tomorrow.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:37.180
Where are they off to…?

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:51.460
Sorry for the short notice.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:55.740
Oh, no, I'm very happy
you're interested in our scallions.

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.160
Are you two athletes?

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:01.680
We work in sales for a beverage company,

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:04.640
but we're also on
the company's badminton team.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:09.680
Got your hands in a lotta pies then?
Must be nice.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:15.300
It's huge!

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.880
This entire field is ours.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.320
Wow…

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:22.620
Fukaya used to be
Japan's number one scallion producer.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:27.900
The fertile soil from the
Tone river and the winter wind

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:30.960
make Fukaya scallions sweet like no other.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:32.140
Here!

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:34.500
Freshly picked!

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:35.680
Thank you.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:44.060
It's spicy…?

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:46.260
Well duh, they're raw!

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:50.620
Grandpa!

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:53.400
Oh, Haruki, good to see you.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.300
Adult grade-schoolers!

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:58.180
You're that kid…!

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.680
Why are adults at an elementary school?

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:03.980
You know him?

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:06.640
We met once in front of the gym.

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:08.080
That so?

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:12.660
Nice to meet you, Haruki. I'm Tatsuru.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:15.920
And this is Mikoto. Go easy on us.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.200
Are you one of the adult grade-schoolers?

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:20.480
You see, we're…

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:23.420
Badrymen!

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:32.760
Eat up now.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.480
Have as much as you like!

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.340
Thank you for the meal!

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.580
This is great!

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:45.200
Fukaya scallions have a
unique sweetness to them, don't they?

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:49.440
These are summer scallions.
The winter ones are even sweeter.

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:52.700
They get about as sweet
as melons or tangerines!

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.060
They might as well be fruit!

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:59.760
Not scallions again…
I wanna eat hamburg steak for once.

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:02.120
No whining in front of guests, please.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:05.260
He's young, he can't help it.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:08.220
It's not meat, but try this, why don't you.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.220
It's good!

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:17.140
A scallion and… apple salad?

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:19.240
It's a surprisingly good match!

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:23.780
Apples are capable of
getting rid of that scallion smell.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:26.600
But scallions smell as good as they taste!

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.060
Sure, honey, whatever you say.

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:31.740
Thank you so much.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:35.280
It's a pleasure to cook
for people who eat so much.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.280
You're athletes through and through.

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:41.640
Oh, no, his stomach is just a black hole.

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:49.140
Take it easy while we prepare the truck, boys.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:51.740
Thank you for everything, ma'am.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:59.420
Look at that! Shibusawa will help us
with the Scallion Ginger Ale.

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:02.160
I really hope the next
prototype will be the last one.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:03.140
Hey!

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:06.760
What's in those big bags?

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:09.820
It's stuff for this thing called badminton.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:13.380
I know! It's popular with kids in my school!

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:17.380
But these are completely different
from the ones at school… So cool!

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.920
Wanna play?

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:21.040
Can we?

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.860
One… two.

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:26.820
Three… four.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:33.860
You're a fine Badryman yourself now.

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:37.960
[All-Japan Corporate Badminton Tournament]
[Day 3]

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:40.540
It's finally time!

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:43.620
If we win today, we get to play Unisics.

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:45.300
Tatsu, it's you!

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.240
[Tonozaki Shiryu, 28]
Tonozaki, it's been ages!

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.640
[Tonozaki Shiryu, 28]
Yes, great to see you again.

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:51.080
It's Tomari…

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:53.000
Wow, they look intense…

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:55.700
Alright, boys, say hi!

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:57.780
Good morning!

00:11:58.020 --> 00:11:59.360
Ouch, my ears…

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:03.020
You're as polite as ever!

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:07.940
Azuma…?

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:17.040
Our order might've backfired on us.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.480
Tonozaki isn't on the first doubles team…?

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:26.860
I put Tatsu and Shiratori on the second team
to avoid direct confrontation with Tonozaki.

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:32.880
Tomari specializes in doubles, and Tonozaki and
Gokura are supposed to be their strongest pair.

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:37.580
That's why their strategy has always been
to put both of them on the first team, but…

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:40.020
But it seems they switched partners…

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:43.940
Tachibana Azuma joined
their team just this season.

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:47.500
Oh, he's the same age as Shiratori and Toya.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:51.240
And he's Tonozaki's new partner
on the second doubles team, right?

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:54.160
Why would they break up their strongest team…?

00:12:54.420 --> 00:13:00.660
No idea. Either they want to see how well the
new kid can do while the stakes are low, or…

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:05.380
They're the new strongest pair…?

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:08.360
Why…?

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.480
What about your elbow…?

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:15.500
That's him, isn't it?

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:16.860
He's your old partner.

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:19.920
Hey, Gokura.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:22.340
[Gokura Kotetsu, 28]
What happened to Tonozaki?

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:23.380
[Gokura Kotetsu, 28]
Tono's…

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:26.040
I'm Tetsu's new partner!

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:30.120
[Saruhashi Yukei, 24]
I'm Saruhashi Yukei. Got a problem with that?

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.360
You wanna go?!

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:32.720
Yukei.

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:37.600
I'm sorry, Tetsu,
should I get into formation? I'll go do that!

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:38.980
What's their deal…?

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:41.640
Love-all. Play!

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:56.140
My bad, I…

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:00.460
Alright!

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:03.820
Time to go all out again!

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:06.440
Everybody, make some noise!

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:12.400
There they are, Tomari's
infamous extreme cheer squad…

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:13.920
Hey, Ko.

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:15.800
N-No, I'm fine!

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:17.180
T-T-This is nothing!

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:36.220
Game. First game won by Gokura and Saruhashi
from Tomari Transport.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:45.280
D'you see that?
D'you see our perfect teamwork?

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:48.660
- Yukei.
- Could he be any louder?

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:51.100
- Sorry, Tetsu!
- Let's focus on our next game.

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:53.800
This isn't a cheering competition anyway.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:56.000
N-No, you're right…

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:00.080
Tomari's cheer squad really is intense!

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:04.700
And they only got louder when the
president's daughter joined the fray.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.560
Man, she's so cool…

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:11.160
This is doing Takeda no favors though…

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:13.160
Love-all. Play!

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:35.460
Stop…!

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:38.000
Please…!

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:41.920
A confession contest…?

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:44.000
Not that it has anything to do with us.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:48.080
But Kawai totally has the hots for Takecchi.

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:48.760
Wha…?

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:50.220
Yeah, I thought so too!

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:52.860
Look, she's looking at us!

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:58.840
See!

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:05.340
Kawai, would you go out with me?

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:08.580
I'm so sorry! I…

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.940
I actually like Yotsuya!

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:29.260
No…! Not now…!

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:37.500
Game. Match won by Gokura Kotetsu
and Saruhashi Yukei from Tomari Transport.

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:43.400
Way to go, Tetsu!

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:48.300
Your smashes are unstoppable!
One day, I hope I can be just like…

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:49.020
Yukei.

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:50.880
I'm sorry, Tetsu!

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:55.840
You always say the game doesn't end
until we thank our opponents.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:57.900
Let's go, let's go!

00:16:58.880 --> 00:16:59.940
Good game!

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:08.720
You can reflect on the game later.
The rest of our team is still fighting.

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:09.480
Yes, sir.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:12.240
[Mashiba Yuho vs. Saeki Sota]

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:13.340
[Mashiba Yuho vs. Saeki Sota]
It's all my fault…

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:15.280
Sorry…

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:17.880
It's not your fault, Ko.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:21.760
Doubles requires two people
and I didn't pull my weight either.

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:25.680
Love-all. Play!

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:26.320
[Mashiba Yuho, 23]

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:28.720
[Mashiba Yuho, 23]
Alright! Serving first gives me an advantage!

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:33.440
Here we go!

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:41.660
How could I mess up there?!

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:44.920
My muscles can do better than this!

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:46.380
Hey, Yuho!

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:50.180
If you lose, I'm never making
you protein shakes ever again!

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:52.020
Miss Ayaka!

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:55.320
I won't lose!

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:00.600
There! I've got this! I can still win!

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:01.460
How…?

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:08.380
How can he be so into it?

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:10.780
He can get as desperate as he wants,

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:14.840
and it won't close the
overwhelming gap in our abilities.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.080
We're almost there…! Just one…

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:24.180
No, two more steps, my thigh muscles!

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:28.900
They can say that
hard work pays off all they want.

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:30.080
- You'll get the next one!

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:31.580
- I know it's not true.
- You'll get the next one!

00:18:32.060 --> 00:18:36.860
There's a million things that your feelings
alone will never be able to change.

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:44.160
Game. Match won by Saeki Sota
from Sunlight Beverage.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:48.640
You completely defeated my muscles!
Good game!

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.660
Well done…

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.700
…is what I'd like to say.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:00.880
Do you even like badminton?

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:03.660
Yes…?

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:06.320
Right…

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:11.980
Sota won, so it's 1-1.
It's all up to the final game now.

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:16.260
Tonozaki and Tachibana only
became partners recently.

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:21.080
Their individual strengths
will play a big role here.

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:25.240
That's your old partner, isn't it?

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:26.140
Yes.

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:28.920
And you guys aren't even gonna say hi?

00:19:30.820 --> 00:19:33.700
Well, who am I to nitpick anyway.

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:37.620
Love-all. Play!

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:49.820
Azuma seemed pretty depressed.

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:51.920
Are you surprised?

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:56.260
How would you react if they told you that you
might not be able to play even after surgery?

00:19:57.080 --> 00:19:59.520
He's been struggling for a while now, too.

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:04.320
Did you know his partner hasn't
even come to check in on him yet?

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:06.700
How could he, after all that?

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:07.980
I know, right?

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.300
He resents me…

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:26.440
…doesn't he?

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.520
I mean, I knew it, but…

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.980
Finally seeing him after all this time…

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:33.940
Mikoto!

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:49.860
Azuma! Azuma! Azuma!

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:52.660
Mikoto, what the hell?!

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:55.480
He'll have to get over it eventually.

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:58.620
This is do or die, Shiratori.

00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:06.840
On it!

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:08.500
Don't tell me…!

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:19.820
11-5.

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:21.900
Interval.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:28.320
If that's how it is…

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:31.980
If that's how it's going to be…

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:35.000
…I wish we hadn't met.
